W tp wire: LOSSY (--tp-wire wht6) at 128 KiB a message and above. A cross-rank all-reduce of that size carries a quantised payload instead of bf16 (libr4d's is Walsh-Hadamard-rotated 6-bit at two ranks and tiered int8 at three and four), so this process does not compute the same function the exact wire does. Steps of at most 25 rows are exact: single-sequence decode, and a decode step until sequences x (1 + speculative depth) passes that; prefill and a busy decode step are lossy. --tp-wire-min-kb moves the floor.
